            'Total points per round: 40',
            'Must win at least 21 points to erase a branch',
            'Kapot (all tricks) erases multiple branches',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize the Aces. Holding two Aces in a 6-card hand makes you nearly guaranteed to capture at least 10 points. If your partner also holds an Ace, you have 20 pointsâ€”just one point shy of winning the round.',
          intermediate: "Trump Defensive: If the opponent chooses trumps, lead low cards in your 'longest' suit to force them to use their trump cards early. If you can exhaust their 6 trump cards, your remaining Aces becomes masters.",
          advanced: "The 'Kapot' Strategy: If your team has high cards in all suits, aim for 'Kapot' (winning all 6 tricks). This erases multiple branches (usually 2 or 3) and is the fastest path to victory.",
          tips: [
            "Always watch which player 'Accepted' the Trump. They are the target for all your defensive leads.",
            "In Kujong, the Queen of Spades (De Mit) is the 'Joker' of the deckâ€”don't lose her to a low Jack.",
          ],
